{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1482267-spiral-walkers-the-sodality-of-the-tor-2e-conversion","id":1482267,"title":"Spiral Walkers (The Sodality of the Tor 2e conversion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-29T10:35:24-07:00","id":1482267,"title":"Spiral Walkers (The Sodality of the Tor 2e conversion)","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sodality of the Tor</span></span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spiral Walkers</i></span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pages 83-94 of Legacies the Sublime for lore</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Path:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Thyrsus</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Order:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Guardians of the Veil or The Mysterium </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fate 2, Occult 2, Shadow Name Merit 1, one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Animal Ken, Crafts, Medicine, or Survival</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiation: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The initiate walks a spiral labyrinth at night while naked and drugged. At the center of the labyrinth they find a cauldron filled with more of the herb infused wine that drugged them originally, they fill their chalice and drink it, releasing the god self for the first time.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcana:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Fate</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> God-self (+1 per Attainment); the full moon (+2); setting aside the conscious mind (+1, +2 if this causes complications, +3 if using supernatural substances).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Spiral dancing; presiding over a ritual feast; walking a labyrinth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainments</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Attainment: Eyes of the Godself</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spiral walkers can become aware of where those around them fall into the archetypes of the gods. After spending a turn interacting with someone, the mage can become aware of their status as oathbreaker, their connections to others, and conditions that befall them. This attainment functions as \u201cInterconnections\u201d (Fate 1, MtAw 134), with reach for instant casting. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Spirit 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The primary resonance also becomes visible to the eyes of the spiral walker. In addition to the information from the attainment above, the mage is able to see the primary resonance of the target.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second Attainment: The Spiral Dance</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate 2, 3 dots in Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The godself is always capable of taking actions that are in the nature of the role they fill. As long as the spiral walker has taken an hour to bring their godself to the surface they do not take untrained penalties on actions that are inline with the nature of the godself\u2019s role. This attainment functions with advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Spirit 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The nature of the godself allows the mage to command entities within the godself symbolic range. This attainment functions as \u201cCoaxing the Spirits\u201d (Spirit 1, MtAw 180) with reach assigned to instant casting and sensory range.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third Attainment: Drawing Down the Moon</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate 3, Shadow Name Merit 2, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 3 or a second option from the list must be raised to 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Sodalites who dance the spiral know what it is to exhaust themselves with drugs and drink and dance until deity declares itself and is born through them, but here the children of Thessaly practice their greatest art and truly draw down the moon and catch it in their cups. This attainment imitates \u201cSworn Oath\u201d (Fate 3 MtAw 137), targeting the mage themself. The promise the mage makes is unspoken but exceptionally clear: They shall become the god. As long as they act in accordance with the god's nature, they receive their boon, and find it refreshed anew at the start of each scene. If used outside of a ritual context or without a suitable ecstatic trance, the attainment only lasts for a number of turns equal to the mage's Fate, after which they suffer a point of Resistant Bashing damage as the strain of forcibly shredding their own ego momentarily wracks them. If used as a part of an ecstatic rite, however, the attainment has Advanced Duration, though the mage must continue to act as the god at all times or face a terrible burden. Most spiral walkers, for that reason, only allow the transformation to last for as long as their high (setting a conditional duration) or until the sunrise or from moon to moon. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Life 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Furthermore, while under the effects of this attainment, the mage takes on the mantle of their god-self far more physically. These alterations vary from the subtle to the grotesque, but it's impossible to ignore. These changes function as \u201cMany Faces\u201d (Life 3, MtAw 150) and they are unrecognizable as being the same person as their mortal self.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fourth Attainment: Selves Intertwined</b> </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate 4, 4 dots of Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The godself and the mage are essentially one being at this point, so close that fate chooses not to see a difference. While under the effect of the attainment Drawing Down the Moon the mage can declare an event that they wish to have happen. So long as it is in line with the nature of the godself, fate will ensure that it happens. This attainment functions as \u201cStrings of Fate\u201d (Fate 4, MtAw 138) with reach for advanced duration. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Spirit 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Finally the spiral walker can call forth entities within their godself\u2019s symbolic nature from beyond the gauntlet. This attainment functions as \u201cSpirit Summons\u201d (Spirit 3, MtAw 182) with reach for advanced duration and to allow the mage to summon spirits on the other side of the gauntlet. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fifth Attainment: Immanent Divinity </b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fate 5, Shadow Name Merit 3, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 4 or a second option from the list must be raised to 3 or a third option must be raised to 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The godself has been fully recognized by this point and can enact its will on the world. This attainment functions as \u201cMiracle\u201d (Fate 5, MtAw 140) with reach for advanced duration. The spiral walker can initiate this attainment while activating the Drawing Down the Moon attainment. The pool of Intercessions refreshes every night when the moon is at its highest point, even if the moon is not visible. The uses of the Intercessions must be in line with the nature of the godself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Life 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spiral walker can take on an animal form that is in line with the symbolic nature of their godself - a god of mazes may take on a rat's form for example, a god of suns could be a hawk. This attainment functions as \u201cShapechanging\u201d (Life 4, MtAw 152) with reach for advanced duration and to allow the mage to remain full control of her human faculties. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-02-2023, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T10:39:52-07:00","id":1482268,"title":"","content":"I don't really know what to say about this legacy. It was weird but the feed back I've gotten from friends says it is good. Someone from Magecord suggested the godself be equivalent to the mages shadow name and we worked around with that. Moving back and forward between spirit and life for optional attainments isn't my favorite, but I wasn't really happy either way with pure life or pure spirit, so the end result was bouncing back and forward.<br /> <br /> In the end, despite a bit holding me back, I think it is a fun legacy, so I'm happy enough to post the end result <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Gotta thank two people from Magecord, Skirgg came up with the oblations and yantras, and Axel, the third attainment is word for word their work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 05-29-2022, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T04:15:05-07:00","id":1482587,"title":"","content":"Oh that is very good.<br /> Thank you, might use on a future game I will run in some months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T04:25:11-07:00","id":1482588,"title":"","content":"Double-Post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}